From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
Date: Wed, 12 Mar 2025 10:28:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libqcow2: fix use-after-free of commit_top_bs in
 commit_abort()

commit_start() hands the CommitBlockJob only a borrowed pointer to
commit_top_bs: the node is kept alive solely by its parents in the block
graph. bdrv_drop_intermediate() reparents those parents onto `base` and
then, on its exit path, drops the last reference to commit_top_bs --
freeing the node even when it returns an error. commit_prepare() forwards
that error, the job transaction rolls back, and commit_abort() then works
on a dangling pointer.

Take a reference of our own before the drop and release it in
commit_clean(), which runs on every finalize path (commit and abort
alike) whenever prepare ran. commit_top_bs then stays valid for the
whole teardown.

Note this bug is not fork-specific: QEMU upstream carries the same
borrowed-pointer pattern (verified identical from v9.1.1 to v10.2.4,
where commit_abort() dereferences s->commit_top_bs->backing->bs
unguarded). It is simply never hit there, because reaching it needs
bdrv_drop_intermediate() to fail *after* its point of no return.

Reproduced deterministically on stock qemu-storage-daemon v9.1.1 + ASan
by committing an intermediate node whose base image path exceeds 1023
bytes, which makes qcow2_co_change_backing_file() reject the backing
filename after the parents have already been reparented.

Signed-off-by: Olivier Lambert <olivier.lambert@vates.tech>
Signed-off-by: Anthoine Bourgeois <anthoine.bourgeois@vates.tech>
---
 qcow2/lib/block/commit.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/qcow2/lib/block/commit.c b/qcow2/lib/block/commit.c
index 7c3fdcb0..fe3f9163 100644
--- a/qcow2/lib/block/commit.c
+++ b/qcow2/lib/block/commit.c
@@ -124,6 +124,13 @@ static void commit_clean(Job *job)
 
     g_free(s->backing_file_str);
     blk_unref(s->top);
+
+    /*
+     * Release the reference taken in commit_start(). On the success path the
+     * filter node is already detached from its parents, so this is the last
+     * reference to it.
+     */
+    bdrv_unref(s->commit_top_bs);
 }
 
 static int coroutine_fn commit_run(Job *job, Error **errp)
@@ -326,12 +333,21 @@ void commit_start(const char *job_id, BlockDriverState *bs,
     commit_top_bs->total_sectors = top->total_sectors;
 
     ret = bdrv_append(commit_top_bs, top, errp);
-    bdrv_unref(commit_top_bs); /* referenced by new parents or failed */
     if (ret < 0) {
+        bdrv_unref(commit_top_bs);
         commit_top_bs = NULL;
         goto fail;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Keep the creation reference for the whole lifetime of the job instead of
+     * relying on the parent links alone: bdrv_drop_intermediate() moves those
+     * parents to base and then drops the last reference, which deletes the
+     * node while s->commit_top_bs still points at it. commit_abort() would
+     * then run on freed memory.
+     * The reference is released in commit_clean() (or in the fail branch of
+     * this function if it fails).
+     */
     s->commit_top_bs = commit_top_bs;
 
     /*
@@ -442,6 +458,11 @@ fail:
         bdrv_replace_node(commit_top_bs, top, &error_abort);
         bdrv_graph_wrunlock();
         bdrv_drained_end(top);
+        /*
+         * commit_clean() does not run for a job that failed to start, so the
+         * reference kept for the job lifetime is released here.
+         */
+        bdrv_unref(commit_top_bs);
     }
 }
 
